      "10.18419/darus-6114",
      "Evaluation of Sliding-Mode Position Controllers on Multi-Axis Machine Tools with Compliant Mechanics"
    ],
    "matched_files": [],
    "scope": "1141 Git-tracked evidence paths, 301 members inside tar.gz, gzip contents and early baseline-index. Case/punctuation/accents normalized. Paper titles used for replication releases."
  },
  "methods": [
    "Parsed 48 axis CSVs and one observer CSV. Checked increasing timestamps, consistent record ID, finite channels, per-axis RMS errors for desired vs load, desired vs motor and motor vs load, torque extrema and recorded velocity setpoints. Position units stay separate for linear x/y/z (µm) and rotary b/c (µrad).",
    "Rebuilt the 3D translational norm independently from x/y/z desired minus load positions for every file publishing e_3d. Flagged absolute disagreement over one nanometre. The separate observer table compares x_des to x_act."
  ],
  "results": [
    "48 five-axis acquisitions (438,000 time rows, 240 axis summaries), including 28 excitation sweeps and three 15,000-row multi-axis control traces. All 48 have 1 ms timestamp spacing. One further observer validation CSV has 9,978 rows.",
    "For lSMC-PI.csv, 760 of 15,000 rows differ by more than 1 nm and the largest discrepancy is 25.40418 µm. The recorded e_3d RMS is 9.24095 µm; recomputing from load positions gives 9.47792 µm. The other 33 files reporting e_3d agree within 1 nm.",
    "Recomputed multi-axis load-error RMS is 23.56365 µm for P-PI, 10.53385 µm for qSMC-PI and 9.47792 µm for lSMC-PI on their respective runs."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This tests agreement with the explicit Cartesian formula, not the cause of the difference in the supplied scalar. Conventions can differ across stages or columns. No documented pre/post limiter pair, drive-limit setting, or directly calibrated external torque transducer. A velocity command and recorded motor torque alone do not identify clipping."
  ],
